  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Decoupled winds at the SFC, clear skies, moist\nlow levels, and saturated soils from MON's rain has already led\nto fog development over SWern zones of the FA. OBS in Duplin and\nInland Onslow County have shown that VIS has already reached \nless than 1mi, 1/4mi in some spots. Have issued a dense fog\nadvisory for these locations, but this may need to be expanded\nNward and Eward in the early morning hours. Drier air is\nexpected to encroach from the W later tonight, which will help\ncut down on fog. Sunrise will aid in burning off the fog, but\nwinds are expected to remain calm into mid morning, so fog will\nlikely linger through the morning commute hours.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Guidance continues to suggest tomorrow will be \nprimarily dry with only an isolated shower or storm possible on \narea breezes in the afternoon. On Wednesday, surface flow \nbecomes more onshore kicking off a period of increasing moisture\nand instability across the Southeast U.S. coastline with a \nmodest uptick of shower and thunderstorm coverage. Another wave \nof low pressure is forecast to lift along the offshore frontal \nboundary Thursday into Friday, pulling it back towards the coast\nand providing a better focal point for more widespread coverage\nof showers and storms into the weekend.",
